# =============================================================================
# SharpLsp .gitignore
#
# One rule per artifact class, filed under the tool that produces it. A pattern
# earns its place only if this repo's build, tests, CI or a contributor's editor
# actually writes that artifact into the working tree. Patterns for toolchains
# we do not use are not free: they hide real files, and nobody ever audits them.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: `.vscode/`, `.idea/` and the per-editor tooling under
# `src/editors/` are shared dev config, and they are committed.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor scratch
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and per-developer machine state
#
# The one section kept on the precautionary principle rather than on evidence:
# nothing here matches anything today, and a miss publishes a credential.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
# Per-machine agent config — leaks local paths and usernames, never publish.
**/settings.local.json
.claude/**/*.local.json
# ...with ONE exception, dug back out because the portfolio standard requires it
# committed: `.claude/settings.local.json` pins `"autoMemoryEnabled": false`.
# Claude Code's local settings file has the highest precedence, so this is the
# only place the value can be pinned for every contributor — and it holds that
# one reviewed key, never machine paths. [GITIGNORE-RULES] [AGENT-AUTOMEMORY]
!.claude/settings.local.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/target
# The Zed extension is a separate cargo workspace with its own target dir.
/src/editors/zed/target/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / VS Code extension
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
out/
*.vsix
.vscode-test/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/
# Where `gh run download` drops the release workflow's outputs (release.yml).
artifacts/
# `dotnet test` without `--results-directory`. Every Makefile target passes one
# (`target/coverage-dotnet`); an ad-hoc run inside a sidecar project does not.
TestResults/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JetBrains Rider plugin (Gradle IntelliJ Platform)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/editors/rider/.intellijPlatform/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# F#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ionide/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coverage
#
# Every gate writes into `coverage/` or under `target/`. The blanket `coverage/`
# rule also swallows the two committed directories that happen to carry that
# name, so they are dug back out — directory first, then contents, because git
# never descends into an excluded directory.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
!.config/coverage/
!.config/coverage/**
!tools/coverage/
!tools/coverage/**

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test output and on-demand fixtures
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Playwright's default output directory (src/website).
test-results/
# Real-world repositories cloned by the VS Code e2e stress suites at pinned
# tags — fetched on demand, never committed (src/.../real-repo-helpers.ts).
/src/fixtures/real-world/
# The same clones from before the repo moved under src/. No code refers to this
# path any more; the rule only stops a stale local checkout being committed.
/real-world-fixtures/

# Scratch projects the VS Code debug suites materialise inside the fixture
# workspace. They MUST live there — VS Code only resolves breakpoints and launch
# targets for files inside an open workspace folder — but they are per-run
# detritus, not fixtures. A crashed or killed run leaks one, and once committed
# its generated sources are globbed into TestFixtures.csproj alongside the next
# run's copy: CS0101/CS0111 duplicate types, and every .NET and VS Code job
# fails at fixture build before a single test runs.
#
# A whitelist, not a prefix list: the suites use two dozen different
# `mkdtempSync` prefixes and add more freely, so naming them individually is a
# race nobody wins. Only the committed fixture directories below are tracked.
/src/editors/vscode/test-fixtures/workspace/*/
!/src/editors/vscode/test-fixtures/workspace/.vscode/
!/src/editors/vscode/test-fixtures/workspace/crosslanguage/
!/src/editors/vscode/test-fixtures/workspace/fsharp/

# Handshake residue from the screenshot suites, which write into the committed
# website assets directory: `<name>.tmp-<pid>.png` plus a `.signal` file next to
# the final PNG (src/editors/vscode/src/test/suite/test-helpers.ts). A killed run
# leaks both into a tracked directory.
/src/website/src/assets/screenshots/*.tmp-*
/src/website/src/assets/screenshots/*.signal

# Google Trends research output: `src/website/tools/trends-research.mjs` drives
# the live explore UI and writes a ~7 MB capture of one run's raw API responses.
# Reproducible on demand, read by nothing in the build; committed once by
# accident, it dwarfed every other file in the repository.
/src/website/tools/trends-results.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent and portfolio tooling
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.too_many_cooks/
.commandtree/
.playwright-mcp/
# Deslop's local index ([CI-DESLOP]) and the reports the CLI writes locally.
.deslop/
deslop-report.*
deslop-*.log

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SharpLsp runtime state
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profiler output; `profiler.output_directory` in src/sharplsp/src/config.rs.
.sharplsp/profiles/
